            <div xml:id="d988">

                <pb facs="1159" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1049"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.79611 Pangborn-Herndon Flight/45:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Forbes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-15T18:00:00+09:00">August 15, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 15—5:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>123. Embassy’s 122, August 15, 4 p.m. I should have stated that their camera and
                    films were confiscated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
